    <!-- 6. Architecture -->
    <section class="section section--bordered" id="architecture">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHead num="04" eyebrow="Architecture" title="One engine, four ways in" lead="One Python server holds the draft state, the engine and a SQLite store. The web panel, the Chrome extension, the MCP server and the terminal all run the same engine." />
        <div class="dc-arch">
          <div class="dc-arch__col reveal" style="--i:0">
            <h4>Sources</h4>
            {sources.map((s) => <div class="dc-node"><b>{s.title}</b><span>{s.text}</span></div>)}
          </div>
          <div class="dc-arrow reveal" style="--i:1" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="draw" viewBox="0 0 36 36" width="36" height="36" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 18h28M23 10l8 8-8 8"/></svg></div>
          <div class="dc-core reveal" style="--i:2">
            <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--plain">Engine</span>
            <h3>Python 3.10+, standard library only</h3>
            <p class="small">Installs with nothing but Python. Twenty-one modules; the ones that matter most are <code>adp</code>, <code>curves</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>opponents</code>, <code>simulate</code>, <code>strategy</code>, <code>engine</code> and <code>explain</code>, which writes the reasoning as deterministic prose.</p>
            <div class="dc-core__mods" aria-label="Modules">{draft.modules.map((m) => <span class="chip">{m}</span>)}</div>
            <div class="dc-core__foot">
              <div><Icon name="database" size={18} /><span><b>SQLite store</b> of every observed draft, feedback and user overrides.</span></div>
              <div><Icon name="cpu" size={18} /><span><b>Optional LLM layer</b> (Ollama, Anthropic or OpenAI): it rephrases, it never decides. Without a model the panel runs entirely on the built-in parser.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="dc-arrow reveal" style="--i:3" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="draw" viewBox="0 0 36 36" width="36" height="36" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 18h28M23 10l8 8-8 8"/></svg></div>
          <div class="dc-arch__col reveal" style="--i:4">
            <h4>Surfaces</h4>
            <div class="dc-node"><b>Web panel</b><span>Served by the same process; the hosted app lives at /app.</span></div>
            <div class="dc-node"><b>Chrome extension</b><span>Manifest V3. An iframe of the panel docked beside the draft room: reads nothing, clicks nothing.</span><button class="link dc-node__link" type="button" data-dialog-open="extension">Permissions and limits</button></div>
            <div class="dc-node"><b>MCP server</b><span>18 tools, so Claude can run the whole draft in conversation.</span><button class="link dc-node__link" type="button" data-dialog-open="mcp">The 18 tools</button></div>
            <div class="dc-node"><b>CLI</b><span><code>ffbot connect | mock | drafts | review | strategy</code></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="dc-shots" data-tabs>
          <div class="dc-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Screenshots">
            {shots.map((s, i) => (
              <button class="dc-tab" role="tab" id={`shot-tab-${s.id}`} type="button" data-tab-target={`shot-${s.id}`} aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls={`shot-${s.id}`} tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1}>{s.tab}</button>
            ))}
