    </section>

    <!-- Accounts band -->
    <section class="dc-accounts" aria-labelledby="accounts-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="dc-acct">
          <div class="reveal">
            <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__num">05</span><span class="eyebrow__slash">/</span><span>Accounts</span></span>
            <h2 id="accounts-title">Your drafts, remembered</h2>
            <p class="dc-acct__lead">Sign in with Google and every draft you run, mock or real, is archived to your account: every pick, every recommendation, your notes. Sleeper offers no sign-in of its own, so Sleeper accounts are linked by username; nothing sensitive depends on it. Accounts are optional, and everything else works without one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dc-acct__rows reveal" style="--i:1">
            <div class="dc-acct__row"><h3>Draft archive</h3><p>Every pick, every recommendation the engine made, and every note typed mid-draft, kept per draft and reopened from the account menu.</p></div>
            <div class="dc-acct__row"><h3>Review chat</h3><p>Ask about a finished draft in plain English, "where did I lose value?", and get an answer from that draft's actual record.</p></div>
            <div class="dc-acct__row"><h3>It learns your style</h3><p>Save your strategy and player calls to your profile and every new draft starts from them. Archived drafts sharpen the market model for future picks.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. Honesty box and FAQ -->
    <section class="section" id="honesty">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="dc-honest reveal">
          <div class="dc-honest__col">
            <Icon name="eye" />
            <h2>It shows its work</h2>
            <p>Every suggestion is a scored breakdown you can expand: projection versus positional replacement, ADP value or reach, tier scarcity, roster fit, injury status, and the simulated odds at your next pick.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="dc-honest__col">
            <Icon name="shield" />
            <h2>It never makes a pick</h2>
            <p>No code path can submit a pick. The Sleeper client is read-only, the extension injects only an iframe, and the model's job ends at a recommendation. You read, you ask, you pick.</p>
